  },
  {
   "v": "dean",
   "t": "Я внимательно слушаю вас, Марина.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's see how Eduard Valentinovich welcomes Marina to the department.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "dean",
   "t": "Наше знакомство началось как-то неправильно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Our acquaintance started somehow wrong.' Eduard tries to smooth over their awkward first meeting at the university.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "dean",
   "t": "Я хочу официально поздравить вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I want to officially congratulate you.' Putting on his most courteous administrator voice, he welcomes her to the staff.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "dean",
   "t": "Наш коллектив маленький, но очень дружный.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Our collective is small, but very friendly.' In Russian workplaces, \"kollektiv\" is the classic word for the whole office team.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "dean",
   "t": "Если будут вопросы — милости просим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'If there are questions, you are welcome.' \"Milosti prosim\" is an old-fashioned, courtly Russian phrase meaning \"you are most welcome\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "dean",
   "t": "Мы всегда находимся в творческом поиске.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
